{
    "background_story": "Ryland was a man of routine, valuing predictability above all else. Every day, he woke up at exactly 6:00 AM, had a bowl of oatmeal for breakfast, and took a 30-minute walk around the block. His job as an accountant suited him perfectly, as he spent most of his days staring at spreadsheets and crunching numbers. Ryland's love for unvariedness extended to his social life, where he met the same group of friends at the same coffee shop every Friday evening. His friends often teased him about his lack of spontaneity, but Ryland wouldn't have it any other way. He found comfort in the familiar rhythms of his life, and the thought of deviating from his routine made him anxious. As he often said, 'Why fix what isn't broken?' Ryland's life may have been uneventful to some, but to him, it was a symphony of predictability and stability.",
